'd go with option 3. Both target versions were healthy in production, so neither rollback needs change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01U22yuRwpsEaaYoSwic4JuZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WF11YSvzMveVR7ScAZyJGJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (deployed this morning to us-east, us-west, eu-west) is unhealthy with an ~18% error rate. payments-api (v5.1.0, degraded, ~18% errors) is impacted downstream. Mitigation: rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, the last release healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HbnQ9KjDPs9exSmn7QzNx8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014fcqUdYWDrJeLx7nxhURnP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2. The worker is healthy again, but payments-api still isn't.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's healthy and its error rate fell from about 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, payments-worker), which paged on-call. The summary says v3.4.0 is the cause, payments-api is affected downstream, and we rolled back to v3.3.0.\n- **payments-api:** It's still on v5.1.0, still unhealthy and still at about an 18% error rate, even after the worker rollback.\n  - The fix may just need more time to reach it, for example while a backlog clears or clients retry.\n  - Or v5.1.0 has its own problem. It was already marked degraded in the release history.\n\nPlease check payments-api again in a few minutes. If its errors don't drop, its own rollback to v5.0.0 (its last healthy release) is the next thing to try. I haven't done that because you said to roll back only the worker. Just say if you want me to.", "type": "text"}]}]}